# Ubuntu Xvfb/GLX: two 128-byte reallocations during glXQueryExtensionsString.
# Observed in CI 42829814334, job 129876608971, with unloaded provider frames.
# Match only that extension-query stack, not InitWindow or Malvado allocations.
leak:extensionSupportedGLX
# Pixel fixtures keep provider modules mapped so their allocations can be named.
# Driver-owned caches are outside Malvado ownership; do not suppress draw frames.
leak:libgallium
leak:/dri/
leak:libLLVM
